window.docContents[90].resolve({"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___3___-The-Cartan-matrix-of-a-finite-dimensional-algebra/Cartan-matrix/#Chapter9___Definition9___3___1":{"contents":"Definition 9.3.1. The matrix C = (c_{ij}) is called the Cartan matrix of A.\n\nObviously, the Cartan matrix of A is a matrix with nonnegative entries, whose diagonal entries are positive.\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t9. Structure of finite dimensional algebras\t9.3. The Cartan matrix of a finite dimensional algebra\tCartan matrix","header":"Cartan matrix","id":"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___3___-The-Cartan-matrix-of-a-finite-dimensional-algebra/Cartan-matrix/#Chapter9___Definition9___3___1"},"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___5___-Orthogonality-of-characters/Idempotents-from-characters-in-the-group-algebra/#Chapter4___Problem4___5___2":{"contents":"Problem 4.5.2. Let G be a finite group. Let V_i be the irreducible complex representations of G.\nFor every i, let\n\n\\psi_i = \\frac{\\dim V_i}{|G|} \\sum_{g \\in G} \\chi_{V_i}(g) \\cdot g^{-1} \\in \\mathbb{C}[G].\n\n(i) Prove that \\psi_i acts on V_j as the identity if j = i, and as the null map if j \\neq i.\n\n(ii) Prove that \\psi_i are idempotents; i.e., \\psi_i^2 = \\psi_i for any i, and \\psi_i \\psi_j = 0 for any i \\neq j.\n\nHint: In (i), notice that \\psi_i commutes with any element of k[G] and thus acts on V_j as an intertwining operator. Corollary 2.3.10 thus yields that \\psi_i acts on V_j as a scalar. Compute this scalar by taking its trace in V_j.\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t4. Representations of finite groups: Basic results\t4.5. Orthogonality of characters\tIdempotents from characters in the group algebra","header":"Idempotents from characters in the group algebra","id":"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___5___-Orthogonality-of-characters/Idempotents-from-characters-in-the-group-algebra/#Chapter4___Problem4___5___2"},"/7___-Introduction-to-categories/7___9___-Exact-functors/#chapter-07___section-7-9":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t7. Introduction to categories","header":"7.9. Exact functors","id":"/7___-Introduction-to-categories/7___9___-Exact-functors/#chapter-07___section-7-9"}});
